[2026-08-12T08:27:25.290Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=a493def3e1aff66f55b19a21ad679d9d]   Trigger:   The user wanted a complete authentication system for the job application agent app, supporting email/password login, Google sign-in, a protected dashboard reachable only after login, and modern sign-in/sign-up pages.
[2026-08-12T08:27:25.290Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=a493def3e1aff66f55b19a21ad679d9d]   Response:  - Implemented Supabase browser, server, and route-protection utilities (client, server, and middleware helpers under the app's Supabase library folder) along with a top-level middleware file that refreshes sessions and redirects unauthenticated users away from the dashboard and authenticated users away from sign-in/sign-up.
- Built email/password and Google OAuth sign-in and sign-up flows using new form components and a shared split-panel auth layout, plus an auth callback route that exchanges OAuth/email confirmation codes for a session and redirects to the dashboard.
- Added a database migration creating a profiles table with row-level security policies and an automatic trigger that provisions a profile row whenever a new user signs up, plus a setup guide documenting how to enable Email and Google providers and configure redirect URLs in the Supabase dashboard.
[2026-08-12T08:27:25.290Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=a493def3e1aff66f55b19a21ad679d9d]   Decisions: - **Split work between local scaffolding and hosted configuration**: Because the AI assistant's Supabase management connector was unavailable in one session, provider enablement (Google OAuth credentials, redirect URLs) had to be documented as a manual dashboard step rather than automated, while the code-level auth flow, middleware, and database migration were still fully built and made ready to apply.
- **Constrain post-login redirect targets to local paths**: Redirect URLs passed through the callback route and sign-in form are validated to start with a single slash and not begin with a double slash, preventing open-redirect style vulnerabilities where a crafted link could send a signed-in user to an external site.
- **Auto-create user profiles via a database trigger rather than app code**: Provisioning a profile row at the database level when a new user is created ensures every user (whether via password or Google sign-up) gets a consistent profile record without relying on client-side code to remember to create one.
[2026-08-12T08:27:25.290Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=a493def3e1aff66f55b19a21ad679d9d]   Todo:      Google OAuth provider credentials and redirect URLs still need to be manually configured in the Supabase dashboard and Google Cloud Console before Google sign-in will work end-to-end.
[2026-08-12T08:27:25.290Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=a493def3e1aff66f55b19a21ad679d9d] Topic: Design clean sign-in and sign-up page layouts
[2026-08-12T08:27:25.290Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=a493def3e1aff66f55b19a21ad679d9d]   Trigger:   The user asked for a clean, modern UI/UX for the sign-in and sign-up pages.
[2026-08-12T08:27:25.290Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=a493def3e1aff66f55b19a21ad679d9d]   Response:  - Created a shared authentication layout component with a dark branding panel on desktop and a card-based form on the right, used by both the sign-in and sign-up pages.
- Added supporting UI primitives (field groups, spinners, separators) and a landing page with call-to-action buttons linking to sign-up and sign-in.
[2026-08-12T08:27:25.291Z] INFO  [QueueWorker] [trace=a493def3e1aff66f55b19a21ad679d9d]   Decisions: A split-panel layout (branding on one side, form on the other) was chosen to give the authentication pages a polished, product-like feel on desktop while collapsing gracefully to a single-column form on mobile, balancing visual appeal with simplicity of implementation.
